/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- THE PAPER'S OWN MODEL, mirrored rather than
  substituted for.

  Klemola & Ilme (IECR 35 (1996) 4579) state the thermodynamics they used:
  liquid activity coefficients by UNIFAC, vapour pressures by Antoine, vapour
  fugacity by the ORIGINAL Soave-Redlich-Kwong.  All three are public in this
  tree, so the case declares exactly them.  A comparison against a measured
  column is worth something only if the model is the one the source used; had
  this dict declared ideal vapour or a fitted NRTL pair, any agreement would
  have been agreement between two different questions.

  ANTOINE lives on each component's own record (`vaporPressure { model Antoine;
  ... }` in data/standards/components/<name>.dat) -- it is a per-component fact
  and is not selected here.  UNIFAC and SRK are the two model slots below.

  UNIFAC coverage, verified rather than assumed.  All nine components carry a
  `groups { unifac ( ... ) }` decomposition:

      propane        2 CH3 + 1 CH2                 nButane      2 CH3 + 2 CH2
      isoButane      3 CH3 + 1 CH                  isopentane   3 CH3 + 1 CH2 + 1 CH
      neopentane     4 CH3 + 1 C                   nPentane     2 CH3 + 3 CH2
      1Butene        1 CH3 + 1 CH2 + 1 CH2=CH
      isoButene      2 CH3 + 1 CH2=C
      trans2Butene   2 CH3 + 1 CH=CH

  Two main groups appear, CH2 and C=C, and the interaction pair between them
  (a = 86.02 / -35.36) is present in data/standards/parameters/UNIFAC/
  interactions.dat.  Nothing is missing, so there is NO approximations{} block:
  every component here is priced by the model that is declared, and an
  authorisation carried over out of habit would read, to anyone auditing the
  answer, as though something had been waved through.

  WHAT THIS SYSTEM IS.  Nine saturated and unsaturated C3-C5 hydrocarbons: the
  mixture is nearly ideal and UNIFAC returns activity coefficients close to 1
  throughout.  That is deliberate and it is the point of choosing this column as
  the corpus's first measured distillation anchor -- what is under test is the
  COLUMN model, and a disagreement cannot be shifted onto the activity model
  and then forgotten.  The separation is hard for a different reason: the keys'
  relative volatility is about 1.40, which is why the plant needs 74 trays and
  a reflux ratio of 11.4.

  PROVENANCE CAVEAT, machine-announced and repeated here.  Seven of the nine
  records (isoButane, 1Butene, isoButene, trans2Butene, neopentane, isopentane,
  nPentane) carry `reviewStatus interim` -- imported from CoolProp 7.2.0 and
  not yet checked against primary sources.  The engine raises this on every
  run.  The thermodynamics beneath this anchor is not itself anchored, and no
  agreement below should be read as validating it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components
(
    propane
    isoButane
    nButane
    1Butene
    isoButene
    trans2Butene
    neopentane
    isopentane
    nPentane
);

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaPhi;

    liquid
    {
        activityModel { model UNIFAC; }     // the paper's liquid model
        standardState pureLiquid;
    }

    vapour
    {
        fugacityModel SRK;                  // the paper's vapour model
    }
}
